    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Bennetts Auctioneers are delighted to bring No. 40 Farney Park to the market. Ideally situated on Farney Park and minutes from Sandymount Village, No. 40 could not ask for a more convenient and enviable location. The property has been well maintained in original condition and has potential to extend subject to planning permission. The accommodation of c. 114 sq. m. briefly comprises of entrance hallway, drawing room, living room, kitchen/dining room, sunroom and W.C. on the ground floor. On the first floor there are three bedrooms and family bathroom. Features of the property include gas fired central heating, convenient side access to rear garden through garage and a private and secluded 70ft rear garden. \r\n\r\nExternally to the front there is off street parking for two cars on a pebbled driveway bordered by stone walls and matured shrubbery. To the rear there is a private and secluded 70 ft garden laid out in lawn with a concrete patio area.\r\n\r\nViewing highly recommended. \r\n\r\nLOCATION\r\n\r\nNestled between Sandymount Road and Claremont Road, No 40 Farney Park is ideally positioned in a highly sought after and convenient location. Within a gentle stroll of Sandymount Village with all amenities including shops, boutiques, restaurants and cafes. The Aviva Stadium and R.D.S. are within a gentle stroll and the East Link bridge is close by providing quick access to Dublin Airport. No. 40 is located just a short distance from the City Centre, IFSC, Silicon Docks and Sandymount Strand. There are a range of primary and secondary schools close by such as Star of the Sea BNS, Lakelands GNS, Educate together, St Matthews, St. Michael's College and Alexandra College. UCD and Trinity College are also within easy reach."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Ground Floor\r\n\r\nEntrance Hall:  4.24m x 1.96m  wood flooring, coving \r\n\r\nDrawing Room:  3.47m x 3.98m  wood flooring, coving, bay window,  \r\n\r\nLiving Room:  3.98m x 3.98m  wood flooring, coving, original feature fireplace, doors to\r\n        \r\nSun Room:  3.56m x 2.87m  wood flooring \r\n\r\nKitchen/ Dining Room:  2.64m x 3.77m  tiled flooring, coving, bay window, range of floor and eye level units, tiled splashback, stainless steel sink, plumbed for washer/ dryer\r\n\r\nInner Hall: 0.99m x 1.60m  tiled flooring\r\n\r\nW/C:  0.82m x 1.60m  half tiled walls, W.C., W.H.B.    \r\n\r\n\r\nFirst Floor \r\n\r\nLanding:  2.85m x 2.45m  carpet flooring, dado rail \r\n\t\t\t \r\n Bedroom 1:  3.96m x 3.46m carpet flooring, bay window, built in wardrobes  \r\n\r\nBedroom 2:  3.75m x 3.63m  carpet flooring, built in wardrobes, window to rear  \r\n\r\nBedroom 3:  3.07m x 2.64m  wood flooring, built in wardrobes, window to front \r\n\r\nBathroom:  1.78m x 2.45m  half tiled walls, walk in shower unit, W.H.B.,W.C. window to rear  \r\n\r\n\r\nTotal Floor Area – c. 114 sq. m. \r\n\r\nExterior\r\n\r\nTo the front there is off street parking for two cars on a pebbled driveway while to the rear a private and secluded 70ft garden laid out in lawn with raised decking area"
      },
